WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:05.952
Howdy! Long ago lots of folks wanted a new life.

2
00:00:05.953 --> 00:00:09.575
So they headed way out west.

3
00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:15.087
This story is about two of them.

4
00:00:15.088 --> 00:00:25.735
Their tale begins in a crowded city.

5
00:00:25.736 --> 00:00:28.478
"Thief!" a mink shouted.

6
00:00:28.479 --> 00:00:31.894
"You stole my pearl necklace!"

7
00:00:31.895 --> 00:00:37.251
The thief was a cat named Cleo.

8
00:00:37.252 --> 00:00:41.433
She darted down the street, smiling.

9
00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:46.749
But as she turned a corner, that smile disappeared.

10
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:50.484
Roscoe was blocking her path.

11
00:00:50.485 --> 00:00:54.217
That dog was the toughest cop in town.

12
00:00:54.218 --> 00:00:58.416
"You're under arrest, Cleo."

13
00:00:58.417 --> 00:01:04.927
"No way, Roscoe!" Cleo yelled and ran the other way.

14
00:01:04.928 --> 00:01:07.735
She looked back.

15
00:01:07.736 --> 00:01:09.947
Roscoe was behind her.

16
00:01:09.948 --> 00:01:13.910
Cleo ran faster.

17
00:01:13.911 --> 00:01:17.788
She turned a corner and slipped through an alley.

18
00:01:17.789 --> 00:01:22.692
"Whew!" Cleo said. "I lost him!"

19
00:01:22.693 --> 00:01:26.282
She turned down another alley.

20
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:30.256
She ran past some barrels and stopped.

21
00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:33.670
"Oops! This is a dead end!"

22
00:01:33.671 --> 00:01:37.734
Cleo spun around and gulped.

23
00:01:37.735 --> 00:01:40.249
"Roscoe!"

24
00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:44.734
"You're trapped, Cleo," the dog said.

25
00:01:44.735 --> 00:01:51.043
Cleo sighed and handed over the necklace.

26
00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.998
"You caught me.

27
00:01:52.999 --> 00:01:56.667
But I'll have better luck next time."

28
00:01:56.668 --> 00:02:00.519
"There won't be a next time," Roscoe said.

29
00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.976
"You're going to jail."

30
00:02:02.977 --> 00:02:05.791
Cleo's shoulders slumped.

31
00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:11.638
Roscoe smiled. "And I'm catching the next train out west."

32
00:02:11.639 --> 00:02:14.050
That was a surprise.

33
00:02:14.051 --> 00:02:17.565
"West?" Cleo said.

34
00:02:17.566 --> 00:02:23.221
Roscoe nodded. "A little town called Prickly Pear needs a sheriff.

35
00:02:23.222 --> 00:02:26.730
Maybe I'll get some peace and quiet for a change."

36
00:02:26.731 --> 00:02:30.390
"When are you leaving?" Cleo asked.

37
00:02:30.391 --> 00:02:33.286
"Now," Roscoe said.

38
00:02:33.287 --> 00:02:35.602
"I was on my way to the train station.

39
00:02:35.603 --> 00:02:40.902
But then I saw you steal the necklace."

40
00:02:40.903 --> 00:02:43.357
He grabbed her paw.

41
00:02:43.358 --> 00:02:48.634
"Let's go. The train leaves soon. I don't have much time."

42
00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:53.632
They walked to the police station.

43
00:02:53.633 --> 00:02:58.953
Cleo saw his train ticket and had a sneaky idea.

44
00:02:58.954 --> 00:03:02.888
As they passed an apple cart, Cleo grabbed an apple.

45
00:03:02.889 --> 00:03:05.386
She tossed it in the air.

46
00:03:05.387 --> 00:03:08.552
It landed on Roscoe's hat.

47
00:03:08.553 --> 00:03:14.058
The apple seller frowned. "You have to pay for that!"

48
00:03:14.059 --> 00:03:17.020
"Huh?" Roscoe said.

49
00:03:17.021 --> 00:03:21.303
"You have one of my apples," the seller said.

50
00:03:21.304 --> 00:03:26.703
"He's right," Cleo said. "It's on your hat."

51
00:03:26.704 --> 00:03:30.272
"How did it get up there?" Roscoe said.

52
00:03:30.273 --> 00:03:35.095
As Roscoe reached up, Cleo grabbed his train ticket.

53
00:03:35.096 --> 00:03:39.899
Then she ran fast.

54
00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.474
At the train station, a whistle blew.

55
00:03:43.475 --> 00:03:46.140
"The train!" Cleo thought.

56
00:03:46.141 --> 00:03:52.332
"It's leaving the station!"

57
00:03:52.333 --> 00:04:00.539
Cleo hopped on and gave her ticket to the conductor.

58
00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:06.959
She sat down and let out a long breath. "Whew!"

59
00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.386
Then she heard a shout.

60
00:04:11.387 --> 00:04:14.444
Out the window she saw Roscoe.

61
00:04:14.445 --> 00:04:27.825
The poor dog was trying to catch the train!

62
00:04:27.826 --> 00:04:37.942
Cleo laughed as the train sped up.

63
00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:46.906
She was headed west.

